CHAPTER.VERS:
But there arose false prophets also among the people, as among you

          {+}
         also there will be false teachers, who will secretly bring in destructive heresies, denying even the Master that bought them, bringing on themselves swift destruction.

And in greed they will with feigned words make merchandise of you

          {+}
        : whose sentence now from of old does not linger, and their destruction does not slumber.

suffering wrong as the wages of wrongdoing; [men] that count it pleasure to revel in the daytime, spots and blemishes, reveling in their deceptions while they feast with you

          {+}
        ;
